{"id": "EUVD-2026-104403", "enisaUuid": "258ec3be-5f5e-3acb-8e71-ede981132542", "description": "Crawl4AI from 0.8.7 through 0.9.5 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in the Docker API server that allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass destination checks via URL userinfo parsing differences. Attackers can set fetch_ssl_certificate=true with crafted userinfo URLs so SSLCertificate.from_url connects to internal hosts on port 443, probing reachability and leaking certificate details.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T15:28:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:33:37", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai/pull/2304", "https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai/blob/v0.9.5/crawl4ai/ssl_certificate.py", "https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai/blob/v0.9.5/crawl4ai/async_crawler_strategy.py", "https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai/blob/v0.9.5/deploy/docker/utils.py", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/crawl4ai-0.8.7-through-0.9.5-ssrf-bypass-via-sslcertificate-from-url-url-userinfo"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vjf2-p5h6-wg3v", "CVE-2026-112363"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f2e08cf2-b98a-3395-943d-0750577f9cc9", "product": {"name": "Crawl4AI", "vendor": {"name": "unclecode"}}, "product_version": "0.8.7 \u22640.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "aee8d29b-c46d-3147-adce-447b7227852f", "vendor": {"name": "unclecode"}}], "isExploited": false}